.TH FU 1 "September 2026" "FU Terminal 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fu \- local-first terminal intelligence, safety, learning, and diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fu
.RI [ --auto ] " request"
.br
.B fu investigate disk
.br
.B fu evidence
.br
.B fu verify last
.br
.B fu why-last
.br
.B fu learn
.I topic
.br
.B fu selftest
.SH DESCRIPTION
FU Terminal resolves terminal requests through deterministic knowledge before using a local Ollama model. Commands are mechanically validated and evaluated by a centralized safety policy before execution. Model-generated commands always require approval; high-risk model-generated commands are blocked.
.SH SAFETY
Only deterministic read-only rules explicitly marked for automatic execution can run under --auto. Curated destructive rules require explicit approval. Unknown or model-generated high-risk commands are hard blocked.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B investigate disk
Read-only filesystem and Kubernetes pressure investigation with evidence and confidence.
.TP
.B evidence
Collect current authoritative local evidence.
.TP
.B verify last
Independently verify the goal of the last recorded command where a verifier exists.
.TP
.B history
Show structured execution history.
.TP
.B incident last
Show the last execution and matching verification evidence.
.TP
.B why-last
Explain the last successful command locally.
.TP
.B learn TOPIC
Teach a command/topic using curated knowledge, TLDR, man/info, and local examples.
.TP
.B selftest
Run FU's regression suite without executing destructive test strings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FU_MODEL
Ollama fallback model. Default: qwen2.5-coder:3b.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Ollama API endpoint. Default: http://127.0.0.1:11434.
.TP
.B FU_WORKSPACE
Workspace root. Default: ~/Desktop/FU-Workspace.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/fu-terminal
installation directory
.br
.I ~/Desktop/FU-Workspace
runtime workspace, logs, sessions, and generated artifacts
.SH AUTHOR
Richmack
